{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And your gift shall be reckoned to you as grain from the threshing-floor.</b> Your terumah of tithe is forbidden to outsiders and to the impure, and one is liable for it death and a fifth — like great terumah, which is called רֵאשִׁית דָּגָן מִן הַגֹּרֶן." "<b>And as the fullness from the winepress.</b> Terumah of wine and oil taken from the winepresses." "<b>Fullness.</b> A term of ripening — produce that has become full." "<b>Winepress.</b> It is the pit in front of the winepress into which the wine flows down. And every term of יֶקֶב is a digging of ground, and so too ״יִקְבֵי הַמֶּלֶךְ״ (Zechariah 14) — that is the ocean, a digging that the King of the world dug."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:35.024804213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}